This is Axcient's fork of the FreeBSD Ports Collection.  Proprietary FreeBSD
ports are stored here.

Sync procedure
==============

This repository should be kept in sync with upstream
(https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-ports).  The procedure to do that is:

```sh
git fetch upstream master
git checkout master
git merge upstream/master
git push origin master
```

Under no circumstances cherry-pick from upstream/master to master!  That will
break merge history, because git is incapable of tracking the source of a
cherry-pick.

Local changes
=============

Local changes may be made as usual.  Either push directly to the master branch,
or make a pull request from another.

The Staging Branch
==================

The Staging branch is intended to test new versions of a small number of ports
before merging them to master.  It is _not_ intended to test changes to every
single port, like bash, rsync, ssmtp, etc.  As such, the merge flow looks like
this:

```
upstream => master => staging
```

When developing new ports or making local changes to existing ports, the changes
may be committed either to `master` or to `staging`, as testing demands require.
Use `git cherry-pick` to merge changes from `staging` back to `master`.

